    98	
    99	## D3 — ZTF × Kepler delta Scuti (real ZTF light curves, external labels)
   100	
   101	- Labels: Murphy+2019 (VizieR J/MNRAS/485/2380/table1, 14,330 Kepler A/F
   102	  stars; `dSct` flag 0/1/2 — ships its own labeled negative class).
   103	- Amplitude axis: Mo+2026 (J/A+A/710/A245): table2 = 259,883 extracted
   104	  frequencies (SNR>8) for 1,838 delta Scutis → per-star dominant amplitude
   105	  (ppt × 1.0857 → mmag); table1 = confirmed super-Nyquist modes → the
   106	  sub-hour stratum (any confirmed SNF ⇒ real mode above Kepler LC Nyquist
   107	  283.2 µHz ⇒ P < 59 min). This replaces the originally scouted Bowman+2016
   108	  join: Bowman's VizieR table carries no amplitudes; Mo+2026 supersedes it
   109	  (and is itself the published Murphy×Bowman merge, 1,838 stars).
   110	- Roster (`build_d3_roster.py`, rebuilt 2026-08-28 post-G1): gmag ≥ 13.2
   111	  (Murphy/KIC g magnitude — the named saturation proxy), ALL 610 dSct=1
   112	  survivors + ALL 76 dSct=2 (own class, excluded from headline numbers) +
   113	  2,314 dSct=0 negatives as a frozen-seed (20260828) simple random sample
   114	  (inclusion probability 0.317 recorded; sampling_weight column carried into
   115	  every weighted estimate) = 3,000. Amplitude coverage of positives:
   116	  456/610 with dominant amplitude; 48 > 10 mmag; 254 in 1–10; 154 < 1;
   117	  290 sub-hour; median 1.77 mmag. The 1–10 mmag log ladder and the
   118	  sub-threshold majority make the completeness turn-on curve the headline
   119	  D3 deliverable, not a defect (pre-registered: risk 2).
   120	- Acquisition: frozen `fetch_catalog_lightcurves.py --roster roster_d3.csv`
   121	  verbatim (10″ cone, 1.25 s cadence, resumable); frozen QC chain via
   122	  `build_panels_generic.py` (nearest-cluster crossmatch, catflags/chi cuts,
   123	  ≥20 exp/band, BJD_TDB at Palomar — all frozen functions).
   124	- Prespecified subsets: crowding (sep < 1.0″, ≤3 objects in cone),
   125	  near-saturation (g < 14 flagged; g > 14 safe subset).
   126	- Caveat on record: dSct=0 means "not a delta Scuti", not "constant" — the
   127	  D3 negative-class result is a TRIGGER RATE (never called FPR); triggered
   128	  negatives get adjudicated in W4 (plausible real variable vs unexplained).
   129	
   130	## D2 — TESS-truth transplant (DAV signals in real ZTF windows)
   131	
   132	- Truth: Romero+2022 (MNRAS 511, 1574; arXiv:2201.04158; 74 new DAVs,
   133	  TESS Cy1–3) + Romero+2025 (ApJ 984, 112; arXiv:2407.07260; 32 new DAVs,
   134	  Cy4–5). Published per-mode tables: period [s] + amplitude [ppt] + per-star
   135	  FAP(1/1000) limit + 20-s-cadence flags. 2025 revisions apply: NOV
   136	  retractions (TIC 261400271, 804835539, 317620456) and updated mode lists
   137	  for re-observed 2022 objects — latest published solution wins.
   138	- Truth model, not interpolation (`d2_truth_model.py`): DAV P < 240 s is
   139	  super-Nyquist AND past the first sinc null of TESS 120-s data; the mode
   140	  table is evaluated analytically at the template's real `bjd_tdb`.
   141	  Chain: ppt → mag (×1.0857e-3) → de-dilution OFF by default (SPOC PDCSAP is
   142	  crowding-corrected; ON = prespecified variant) → de-integrate TESS sinc
   143	  (reject modes with |sinc| < 0.3, i.e. P < ~160 s from 120-s data; prefer
   144	  20-s cadence solutions) → bandpass ladder A_g/A_TESS ∈ {1.4, 1.7, 2.1} ×
   145	  A_r/A_g ∈ {0.70, 0.80, 0.90} (nominal 1.7/0.80 from an in-code blackbody
   146	  derivative; the ladder is non-optional — zr carries most published
   147	  confirmations) → re-integrate ZTF 30-s sinc analytically → compose
   148	  phase-coherently in zg and zr (shared t_ref) so the frozen two-band rule
   149	  keeps its meaning.
   150	- Windows: templates from ALL 928 stars of the published catalog (G1 fix —
   151	  the earlier 510-not-detected pool conditioned on the pipeline's own
   152	  outcome), matched by median zg mag (|Δg| ≤ 0.25, widened when thin;
   153	  flagged), K=3 per target at 10/50/90th percentile of exposures-per-night
   154	  (75% of zg nights are single-exposure; per-night median subtraction
   155	  annihilates 53% of zg data — pre-registered, stratified: risk 3).
   156	  Native variability in the pool is handled by strict frequency-matched
   157	  scoring plus PAIRED UNINJECTED CONTROLS (95-prefix): one control shard per
   158	  unique arm-B template window. W2 stretch: fetch real ZTF light curves at
   159	  the 103 Romero positions; where the frozen QC crossmatch succeeds, those
   160	  self-windows become the preferred templates (removes template-choice
   161	  conditioning entirely for that subset).
   162	- Arms: B primary (signal + real ZTF mags, real magerr), A diagnostic
   163	  (synthetic Gaussian floor). FPR: 1,000 arm-A zero-amplitude nulls
   164	  (510 not-detected windows, fresh deterministic noise seeds where windows
   165	  repeat — windows repeat, noise does not; documented). Arm-B nulls are
   166	  tautological (templates ARE the not-detected set).
   167	  Verification arm: ~20 SPOC light curves prewhitened to confirm published
   168	  solutions; everything else needs metadata only.
   169	- Run matrix (sized to the 1-day wall budget at 22 workers ≈ 84 stars/h):
   170	  arm B nominal (1.7/0.80) 103×3 templates = 309; arm A nominal 309;
   171	  nulls 1,000; ladder sensitivity = 8 remaining (R_g, R_rg) points × 103 ×
   172	  1 template (the median-n_exp one) = 824. Total ≈ 2,442 ≈ 1.2 d.
   173	  De-dilution variant runs only for the SPOC verification-arm stars (dilution
   174	  factors are not in the papers; CROWDSAP comes with the ~20 downloads).
   175	  Post-G1 additions: paired controls (~<=309, prefix 95) and a phase-draw
   176	  sensitivity axis (2 extra deterministic phase draws x 103 targets on the
   177	  median template, arm B nominal) ≈ +515 runs; total ≈ 2,960 ≈ 1.5 d.
   178	- Truth-model corrections found at implementation (2026-08-28): |sinc| ≥ 0.3
   179	  rejection corresponds to P < ~160 s at 120-s cadence (the earlier "197 s"
   180	  was the |sinc| = 0.5 point); D2 min published period is 115.9 s and 49/103
   181	  stars carry 20-s solutions, so few modes are affected. Phases are
   182	  unpublished: drawn once per star from PCG64(seed=TIC), shared across bands
   183	  and ladder variants. Blackbody derivative at 11,500 K gives (1.43, 0.80) —
   184	  the ladder's low rung; upper rungs cover atmosphere-model/limb-darkening
   185	  uncertainty.
   186	
   187	## Metrics — see METRICS_SPEC.md (frozen before any campaign L-S run)
   188	
   189	## Execution topology
   190	
   191	- Mac: rosters, fetches, shard building, metrics, figures, git (authoritative).
   192	- Laptop `jacks-7i-5090` (22 workers): replay gate + D3 run. Desktop
   193	  (needs wake; offline 64 d): D2 + D3 overflow; if unreachable, D2 runs on
   194	  the laptop after D3 (+1 day; slip rule below).
   195	- Windows job launches escape the sshd job object via WMI
   196	  `Win32_Process.Create` (Start-Process children die with the ssh session —
   197	  found the hard way on the first replay launch).
   198	- Wall model (anchor 928 ≈ 11 h at 22 workers; cost scales with baseline):
   199	  D3@3,000 ≈ 1.2–1.9 d; D2 ≈ 1 d; hard stop via 150-star timing pilot.
   200	  Disk binds, not time: `workers = min(22, floor(free_GB × 0.5 / 0.47))`,
   201	  scratch on local NVMe/RAM disk, never a synced folder.
   202	- Results bundles: `generalization/results/<date>_<dataset>/` mirroring the
   203	  existing convention (README, DATA_PROVENANCE, SHA256SUMS, acceptance.json).
   204	
   205	## Review gates (sol@xhigh + ChatGPT Pro standing directive)
   206	
   207	| Gate | When | Reviewer | Scope |
   208	|---|---|---|---|
   209	| G1 | DONE 2026-08-28 | sol ×3 | 47 findings; dispositions in reviews/G1/RESPONSE.md; design fixes applied same day |
   210	| G2 | end W1 | sol ×5 | this file + METRICS_SPEC.md; frozen only after unanimous/addressed |
   211	| G3 | W2 pre-batch | Pro (inline code) | d2_truth_model + build_d2_shards: sinc algebra, bandpass, phase coherence, schema |
   212	| G4 | W3 mid-run | sol ×2 | pilot metrics sanity, run anomalies |
   213	| G5 | W4 | Pro + fresh-context verifier | results audit; every headline number re-derived from JSONs/CSVs |
   214	| G6 | Sep 26–29 | sol ×3 + ars-abstract | final abstract |
   215	
   216	## Timeline
   217	
   218	- W1 (Aug 28–Sep 3): tag+branch ✓, replay gate ✓(running), env pinning ✓,
   219	  frozen_api+tests ✓, D3 roster ✓, D3 IRSA fetch (overnight, running),
   220	  D2 sources downloaded ✓, PLAN+SPEC (this commit), G1, G2, D2 roster parser.
   221	- W2 (Sep 4–10): build_panels_generic on D3 → census; d2_truth_model + tests
   222	  + G3; build_d2_shards; verify_cli_identity; 150-star pilot; wake desktop.
   223	- W3 (Sep 11–17): D3 full run (laptop) ∥ D2 (desktop); metrics+plots against
   224	  pilot output; G4.
   225	- W4 (Sep 18–25): metrics, ladders, figures, bundles, acceptance; G5;
   226	  cross-dataset synthesis table.
   227	- Sep 26–30: abstract + G6; submit.
   228	- Slip rule (revised at G1 — the old "D2 alone flips the condition" claim is
   229	  untenable since D2 is not an externally labeled sample): D3 is the dataset
   230	  that satisfies the external-label condition; if only ONE new dataset can
   231	  land by Sep 25 it must be D3, with D2 stated as in progress. If only D2
   232	  lands, the abstract is scoped to injection-recovery + D1 and makes no
   233	  external-validation claim.
   234	
   235	## Top risks
   236	
   237	1. Env fails replay → pin/iterate until byte-identical; blocks all work.
   238	2. D3 completeness ≈ 0 below the a95 floor → stratification IS the
   239	   deliverable (turn-on curve).
   240	3. D2 high-pass ≈ 0 from the single-exposure-night penalty → pre-registered
   241	   expected headline, stratified to be explanatory.
   242	4. A_r/A_g lever → mandatory ladder; headline reported as a band.
   243	5. D3 negatives not constants → FPR an upper bound, stated.
   244	6. Desktop unreachable → D2 on laptop after D3 (+1 day).
   245	7. Romero mode tables are LaTeX prose with typos (comma decimals, stray
   246	   units) → parser with hard row-count and range asserts; G3 reviews the
   247	   parsed output against the PDFs.
   248	
   249	## Mandatory citations
